  "issue_number": 3463,
  "issue_title": "Add a network operations leaderboard (serving + prometheus telemetry) to the explorer page",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`GET /api/v1/chain/serving` and `GET /api/v1/chain/prometheus` are live, network-wide axon-serving/telemetry leaderboards with zero UI touchpoint. Both are implemented (`src/chain-serving.mjs`, `src/chain-prometheus.mjs`) and registered in `src/contracts.mjs` \u2014 each returns a per-subnet leaderboard ranked by announcement volume, a network-wide rollup, and an intensity distribution, computed live from the `account_events` D1 tier. Neither has a frontend query function nor any rendering \u2014 the chain explorer page currently shows daily activity, fees, call mix, and top signers/payers, but nothing about which subnets are actively announcing operational endpoints.\n\n## Requirement\n\nAdd a \"Network operations\" leaderboard section to the chain explorer page (`/explorer`) that renders the per-subnet axon-serving and Prometheus-telemetry leaderboards side by side, each with its network-wide rollup stat.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoints:\n  - `GET /api/v1/chain/serving?window=7d|30d&limit=` \u2014 per-subnet axon-serving leaderboard (`src/chain-serving.mjs`, contract at `src/contracts.mjs:3019`)\n  - `GET /api/v1/chain/prometheus?window=7d|30d&limit=` \u2014 per-subnet Prometheus-telemetry leaderboard (`src/chain-prometheus.mjs`, contract at `src/contracts.mjs:3047`)\n  - Response shape (verified in `buildChainServing`/`buildChainPrometheus`): `{ schema_version, window, observed_at, subnet_count, network: { distinct_servers, announcements, announcements_per_server }, intensity_distribution: { count, mean, min, p25, median, p75, p90, max } | null, subnets: [{ netuid, distinct_servers, announcements, announcements_per_server }] }` for serving; the Prometheus mirror uses `distinct_exporters`/`announcements_per_exporter` in place of `distinct_servers`/`announcements_per_server`. Rows are keyed by **`netuid`**, not by account.\n- Query function: **none exists.** Searched `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` for `chainServingQuery`/`chainPrometheusQuery`/any caller of `/chain/serving` or `/chain/prometheus` \u2014 zero hits. The data layer is **not done**. This PR must add both typed query functions, following the existing `chainFeesQuery`/`chainSignersQuery` pattern at `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts:2347-2398` (`queryOptions` + `k(\"chain-serving\", window)` queryKey + `apiFetch<unknown>` + `isRecord`/`firstString`/`firstFiniteNumber` normalization + `normalizeChainRows` for the `subnets` array + `staleTime: STALE_SHORT`), plus the corresponding types in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` (the file already documents the sibling account/subnet-scoped types for serving/prometheus around lines 1164-1227) \u2014 **as well as** the UI wiring described below, both in one PR.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- File to change: `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (confirmed exists, 520 lines) \u2014 add query calls inside `ExplorerDashboard()` (defined at line 225) alongside the existing `useSuspenseQuery(chainFeesQuery(win))`/`useSuspenseQuery(chainSignersQuery(win))` calls at lines 230-233, and add a new section after the existing \"Call mix\" / \"Most active accounts\" row (lines 454-517).\n- Exact anchor: extend the `<div className=\"space-y-10\">` dashboard body in `ExplorerDashboard()`. Reuse the same `win` (`7d`/`30d`) window toggle already wired via `Route.useSearch()`/`navigate` at lines 226-264 \u2014 pass it straight through to the new queries, no new search-param plumbing needed.\n- What to render: a two-column `grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2` section titled \"Network operations\" (matching the existing `<h2 className=\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-muted\">` header style used throughout the file), containing two leaderboard tables modeled directly on the existing \"Top fee payers\" table (lines 401-451): one column header \"Subnet\" (each row a `<Link to=\"/subnets/$netuid\" params={{ netuid: subnet.netuid }}>`, per the established convention in `subnet-price-ticker.tsx`/`subnet-profile-panel.tsx` \u2014 netuid passed as a number, not a string), plus right-aligned columns for the row's volume metric (`announcements`), distinct-endpoint-count metric (`distinct_servers` / `distinct_exporters`), and the per-server/per-exporter intensity ratio. Above each table, surface the network rollup as compact stat text or `StatTile`s (total `announcements`, `distinct_servers`/`distinct_exporters`) the same way the page already surfaces window-scoped totals in the KPI tile grid (lines 267-301). Left table = serving (`chain/serving`), right table = prometheus (`chain/prometheus`).\n- Coordination note: issue #3464 (\"Add an axon-removals 'churn' panel next to the network operations leaderboard\") explicitly anchors itself to this section \u2014 it adds `GET /api/v1/chain/axon-removals` as a third panel beside these two. Leave room (e.g. a `grid-cols-2` that can extend, or a wrapping `<section>` boundary) so that PR can slot in without restructuring this one's markup.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` gains a `chainServingQuery(window)` and `chainPrometheusQuery(window)` following the existing `queryOptions` pattern, and `explorer.tsx` imports and calls both via `useSuspenseQuery` (matching the file's existing Suspense-based convention, not `useQuery`)\n- [ ] The rendered section shows, for both serving and prometheus: a per-subnet leaderboard table (netuid linked to `/subnets/$netuid`, announcement count, distinct-endpoint count, per-endpoint intensity ratio) ranked by announcement volume, plus the network-wide rollup totals\n- [ ] The `7d`/`30d` window toggle already on the page (lines 249-264) drives both new queries\n- [ ] Empty state matches the file's existing convention \u2014 a `<p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">` message (e.g. \"No serving activity in this window yet.\") when `subnets` is empty, exactly as `fees.top_fee_payers.length > 0 ? (...) : (<p>No fee payers in this window yet.</p>)` does at lines 410-450; loading/error states are already handled page-wide by the existing `<QueryErrorBoundary>`/`<Suspense fallback={<Skeleton .../>}>` wrapper (lines 72-76) and need no new per-section handling\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- The axon-removals \"churn\" panel (`GET /api/v1/chain/axon-removals`) \u2014 that is issue #3464, a separate PR\n- CSV export wiring (`?format=csv` is supported by both endpoints but is out of scope here; general CSV-download-button work is tracked separately, e.g. #3402-#3404/#3406-#3409)\n- Per-subnet drill-in views (`/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/serving`, `/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/prometheus`) \u2014 the query functions already exist (`subnetServingQuery`/`subnetPrometheusQuery` at `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts:3105`/`:3136`, with unit test coverage) but have **no UI consumer** anywhere in the codebase today; wiring them into a per-subnet view is a separate, future PR, not this issue. This issue is the network-wide leaderboard only.\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
